# ERRORS.md — project-local failure log

> Drop this file at the root of a new project. Log here when an approach needed >2 attempts to work — what failed, what worked instead, what to remember. adk skills read this before proposing approaches to similar tasks.
>
> This complements (not replaces) two adjacent systems:
> - `~/.agents-devkit/improve/learning/decisions.jsonl` — structured per-fork decisions (machine-read).
> - `MEMORY.md` — narrative decisions and their rejected alternatives.
>
> ERRORS.md is specifically for *approaches that didn't work* and *lessons that aren't yet a project invariant*.

## Entries

### YYYY-MM-DD — <task or symptom in one line>

- **What didn't work:** <approach + why it failed (cite `path:line` or URL if applicable)>
- **What worked:** <approach + why>
- **Lesson:** <one line for future-you>
- **Promote to MEMORY.md?:** <yes/no — if this is now a permanent rule, lift it into MEMORY.md's "Permanent facts">

(newest at the top — when an entry is promoted to MEMORY.md, leave the ERRORS.md entry in place with the promotion noted)

## How to use this file

- Before proposing an approach to a task that smells like a prior failure, **read this file**.
- An entry counts as "active guidance" until it's promoted into MEMORY.md's permanent-facts section or explicitly retired (with a date).
- adk skills SHOULD cite ERRORS.md entries when their plan deliberately avoids an approach logged here ("not doing X because ERRORS.md 2026-04-12 — Y").
